From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saphira forward-port <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [FWD 7.2.9] mm: let bulk and folio allocators carry alloc_flags

Fwd-port of upstream 2b652377 ("mm/page_alloc: let the bulk and folio
allocators carry alloc_flags", Gregory Price, 2026-07-18, series
position 016) onto Linux 7.2.9.

Why needed: the branch base carries akpm 7.3-bound plumbing in which
mm/page_alloc.h holds __alloc_pages_noprof(..., alloc_flags) and struct
alloc_context.alloc_flags. 7.2.9 predates that restructure: there is no
mm/page_alloc.h (decls live in include/linux/gfp.h + mm/internal.h),
__alloc_pages_noprof/__alloc_frozen_pages_noprof take no flags, and
struct alloc_context has no alloc_flags field. This adaptation
introduces the same carrying capability in 7.2.9 shape:
- struct alloc_context += alloc_flags (mm/internal.h) + ALLOC_DEFAULT
- __alloc_frozen_pages_noprof/__alloc_pages_noprof/__folio_alloc_noprof
  += alloc_flags param, threaded into ac and the fastpath flags
- alloc_pages_bulk_noprof split into __alloc_pages_bulk_noprof(zlflags)
  + wrapper (ALLOC_DEFAULT), failover passes zlflags through
- all in-tree callers (slub, mempolicy x4, khugepaged, migrate,
  page_frag_cache x2, gfp.h inline node helpers, non-NUMA stub, nolock
  path) pass ALLOC_DEFAULT/0 or the through-param: behavior-preserving
  (every new arg is 0/DEFAULT except plumbed pass-through).
- the mm/page_alloc.h hunk is redirected to gfp.h/internal.h.
- continuation-line alignment matches the branch revision byte-for-byte
  where later patches (035) reuse the lines as hunk context.
No WARN_ON/validation is added here; flag interpretation
(ALLOC_ZONELIST_PRIVATE/select_zonelist) arrives with fwd-018.

Byte-identical upstream patch retained in series/ (recorded SKIP-FWD).
Verifies with git apply --check (no fuzz).

Signed-off-by: Saphira builder <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
---
